-- Regression test for lexical section scoping — FIX D, sibling shape.
--
-- Two SIBLING sections each define x and each reference it from inside
-- themselves. Both references resolve to their own section's x (spec §3.1:
-- same section first). The first section's reference must not become
-- ambiguous merely because a LATER sibling rebinds the name.
--
-- Previously this reported
--
--     There are multiple definitions for the identifier x
--
-- at line 18 — the reference inside `Title`, i.e. the location of the
-- (spurious) ambiguity, not the rebinding at line 21. Reversing the order of
-- the two sections made the error disappear; see FIX B/FIX D in spec §12.

§ `Title`
x MEANS 1
f MEANS x PLUS 1              -- Title's x

§ `One`
x MEANS 2
g MEANS x PLUS 1              -- One's x

#EVAL f    -- 2
#EVAL g    -- 3
